01 - Neural Arithmetic Logic Units with Two Transition Matrix and Independent Gates (2024)
- REFERENCE CATEGORY: 
- GOOGLE SCHOLAR CITATIONS: 
- PROBLEM: Neural networks have traditionally struggled with systematic generalization when the numerical range at test time differs from the training range
- OBJECTIVE: To build a neural network that actually knows arithmetic, not just one that approximates it within a familiar range.
- DATASET: Two datasets used for different stages: (1) hand-drawn digit images, for image-recognition pretraining/testing. (2) Numeric pairs (a, b) drawn from defined ranges, for the arithmetic task itself. No sample counts recorded — only the range boundaries used for train/test splits.
- MODELS: NAC, NALU, NALU2M, NALUIG, NALU2MIG
- METRICS & RESULTS: 
- CHOSEN MODEL: NALU2MIG
- GAPS: NALU2MIG looks very promising on clean synthetic numbers, but we don't yet know if those gains hold in messier, real-world settings where numbers come from text, images, or code rather than clean numeric inputs.


02 - Characterization of Quantum Computers for Optimal QML in Brain Tumor Classification (2025)
- REFERENCE CATEGORY: 
- GOOGLE SCHOLAR CITATIONS: 
- PROBLEM: 
- OBJECTIVE: To test (1) whether a quantum machine learning model behaves consistently when run on different hardware, and (2) how its performance scales as more features are added.
- DATASET: Kaggle brain tumor MRI dataset — 3,763 medical scan samples with 15 extracted features (things like image texture, contrast, and intensity statistics). No raw MRI images; just the numerical measurements derived from them. Tested across 8 different IBM quantum hardware backends, with feature subsets ranging from 2 to 9 dimensions.
- MODELS: A Quantum Support Vector Classifier (QSVC) was built and tested on real IBM quantum hardware, then compared against a classical Support Vector Classifier (SVC). The quantum model used a ZZFeatureMap to encode data into quantum states and a RealAmplitudes circuit to process it.
- METRICS & RESULTS: QSVC matched classical accuracy at low feature counts (98.5% at 2 features) but collapsed to 44.5% at 9 features, while the classical SVC held above 99% throughout.
